<title>BELGIUM: Royale Belge H1 1996 profit up 13.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Royale Belge H1 1996 profit up 13.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in billion of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net (excludes minorities)	 5.07 vs   4.46</p>
<p>    Cons net					5.1  vs   0.3</p>
<p>    Cons premium income			59.32 vs  57.94</p>
<p>NOTE - Royale Belge is Belgium's second largest insurance company. It is 52.1 percent owned by  Royale Vendome, which is held by French UAP and Belgian holding company Groupe Bruxelles Lambert (GBL).  </p>
<p>    Gross life premiums			22.69 vs 22.18</p>
<p>    Gross non-life premiums		  36.63 vs 35.76</p>
<p>    Banking return Belgium		    3.76 vs  2.83</p>
<p>NOTE - Group net profit of 5.07 billion francs was at the lower end of analysts' forecasts, which ranged from 5.0 to 5.3 billion francs.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
